Subject: MLA: release the unused NoPE query storage before sparse attention

For a NoPE MLA layer (qk_rope_head_dim == 0) the zero-width q_pe slice is still a view of the whole projected
query, so the query could not be freed before the sparse kernel ran. The unused q_nope view is dropped and q_pe
gets its own empty storage when the rope width is zero, so the projected query can return to the allocator
before the attention output is allocated. Layers with a nonzero rope width and the dense paths are unchanged.

Upstream: the same change as dev commit 716533a. Test: tests/mla_query_lifetime_cpu (extracts the real _attend
method and runs it on CPU).

